findings.body:
The PR description says "Added comprehensive test coverage for `useStateFavicon` hook (10 test cases)" and the checklist ticks "includes unit tests that cover the changes". There is no `use-state-favicon.test.ts` in the diff or in the head tree. `src/hooks/` only contains `use-state-favicon.ts`, although the sibling `use-page-title.test.ts` shows the pattern to follow.

The hook has real branching worth covering: the dark vs. light element selection, the `if (stateType)` guard, and the cleanup that resets to default icons.

::file{file="ui-v2/src/hooks/use-state-favicon.ts"}

::code{file="ui-v2/src/hooks/use-state-favicon.ts" lines="37-66"}

`StateType` includes `CANCELLING` and `PAUSED`, but only seven SVGs were added: cancelled, completed, crashed, failed, pending, running, and scheduled. The guard at line 49 only checks that `stateType` is truthy, then builds `/${stateType.toLowerCase()}.svg` unconditionally.

For those two states the href points at `/cancelling.svg` or `/paused.svg`, and neither file exists in `ui-v2/public`. The browser then shows a broken or blank favicon. The checklist says these states "will not update favicon", but the code points the icon at a 404 instead of leaving it alone.

::code{file="ui-v2/src/hooks/use-state-favicon.ts" lines="49-53"}

::callout{type="warning"}
Only set an icon for states that have an asset, or fall back to the default icon.

::suggestion{file="ui-v2/src/hooks/use-state-favicon.ts" lines="49-53"}
const SUPPORTED_ICON_STATES = new Set<StateType>(["SCHEDULED", "PENDING", "RUNNING", "COMPLETED", "FAILED", "CANCELLED", "CRASHED"]);

if (stateType && SUPPORTED_ICON_STATES.has(stateType)) {
  const faviconPath = `/${stateType.toLowerCase()}.svg`;
  favicon16?.setAttribute("href", faviconPath);
  favicon32?.setAttribute("href", faviconPath);
}

The condition changed from `flow_run_name && flow_run_id` to `flow_run_id`, but the link text is still `{taskRun.flow_run_name}`. If the name is null, the anchor contains only an icon with no text.

::code{file="ui-v2/src/components/task-runs/task-run-details/task-run-details.tsx" lines="45-57"}

Either keep the name in the condition, or fall back to the flow run id for the label. The second option keeps the link useful.
